  "record": {
    "read_status": "full",
    "file_problem": "none",
    "relation": "discusses",
    "tranche": "T6",
    "tranche_reason": "The study tests a nested-scenario jailbreak, not fine-tuning, response-position KL, compliant-token prefilling, suffixes or decoding changes, safety localization in weights, or deepening safety training. Its attack results do not test the listed claim versions.",
    "gate_note": "The study reports harmful-response outcomes for its own nested-scenario attack and ablations. These are recorded as findings about jailbreak performance, not as tests of the listed mechanisms. The preliminary feature-score table measures prompt features rather than harmful compliance; baseline-method results attributed to prior work are not included.",
    "test_reason": "The paper proposes a black-box nested-scenario prompt jailbreak (RTS-Attack) and reports its success rates. It has no fine-tuning, per-token KL, prefill/suffix/decoding, weight-localization or deepening experiments. Prompt-level jailbreaks are not the V4 mechanism, which is getting past the opening response tokens. The paper never tests whether bypass depends on early tokens.",
    "authors_conclusion": "The authors conclude that LLM alignment defenses are insufficiently sensitive to nested scenarios that are semantically relevant and contain targeted toxic knowledge, and that RTS-Attack is effective and efficient across the evaluated LLMs. The record's paraphrase is accurate.",
    "recipe": "different",
    "recipe_differences": "This is a black-box prompt-attack framework using generated nested scenarios and customized instructions, not a fine-tuning or response-position KL method.",
    "method_sensitivity": "Attack success varies with whether customized instructions are included and with scenario genre. The preliminary analysis also reports higher success for scenarios with relevance, especially when relevance and toxicity are both present.",
    "fits_no_version": [
      {
        "finding": "A nested-scenario prompt attack that is semantically relevant and carries targeted toxic knowledge, plus a customized instruction, gets 94-99% ASR on six LLMs. Without the customized instruction ASR is 4-10%, and scenario genre changes ASR (94% crime news, 86% myth, 84% sci-fi).",
        "proposed_claim": "A nested-scenario attack combining generated context with customized instructions can elicit harmful responses in the evaluated LLMs; its success depends on the instruction component and scenario genre.",
